(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// ComplexType is complex, with CPython 3.14's arithmetic (Objects/complexobject.c): the mixed-mode"] [11 1 "// rules for a real operand, _Py_c_quot's division with C11's recovery of infinities, c_powi's"] [12 1 "// integer powers."] [15 1 "// Complex is a complex."] [20 1 "// BaseComplex is the complex value of a complex or of a complex subclass's instance."] [23 1 "// NewComplex is the complex of v."] [26 1 "// Value is the complex's value."] [42 1 "// ComplexRepr is repr(complex): \"2j\", \"(1+2j)\", \"(-0-1j)\", with float repr's digits without \".0\"."] [55 1 "// cQuot is _Py_c_quot."] [98 1 "// fm is a product rounded on its own: the conversion forbids the compiler to fuse it with an addition"] [99 1 "// (Go may on arm64; CPython's C, built without contraction, never does), so results are the same on"] [100 1 "// every architecture."] [107 1 "// rcQuot is _Py_rc_quot: a real divided by a complex."] [143 1 "// cPow is _Py_c_pow; ok false is EDOM (zero to a negative or complex power)."] [154 2 "// musl's libm (go/arbace/libm, the user's decision on PY5b's DECISION 1 (a)), as CPython's _Py_c_pow calls it"] [177 1 "// ComplexPow is complex_pow: an integral real exponent up to 100 by squaring, else _Py_c_pow;"] [178 1 "// an infinite result from finite operands an OverflowError."] [201 1 "// complexOperand is o as a complex and whether it is real (an int or a float): 3.14's mixed-mode"] [202 1 "// arithmetic treats a real operand as a real, not as complex(x, 0)."] [345 2 "// float's and int's numeric members at the type level (float.real.__qualname__)"] [365 3 "// actual_complex_new: a single exact complex argument of complex() is returned as it is (queue 537)"] [380 1 "// newComplexSubclass makes an instance of a complex subclass; PY5c sets it (by default the base value: PY5c wraps it)."] [385 1 "// complexArgs is complex(real, imag) or complex(str)."] [413 3 "// actual_complex_new parses a single positional string; complex_new_impl (two arguments, keywords) takes"] [414 3 "// no string (3.14: \"complex() argument 'real' must be a real number, not str\"; queue 537)"] [420 2 "// try_complex_special_method on the real part (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: fractions' Rect): __complex__ is looked"] [421 2 "// up on any type, a complex subclass's too, but for actual_complex_new's single exact complex argument, returned as it"] [422 2 "// is; a strict subclass of complex returned is deprecated (Issue #29894, queue 537)"] [440 2 "// complex_new_impl's DeprecationWarnings (two arguments or keywords: not actual_complex_new's single argument): a"] [441 2 "// complex 'real' (or one made by __complex__) whose own type is no real number, a complex 'imag'"] [442 2 "// complex_new_impl checks both arguments' types, 'real' then 'imag', before it warns"] [506 2 "// complex_new's combination: a part is added only when it came from a complex, so that a zero's"] [507 2 "// sign survives (complex(1.0, -0.0) is (1-0j); REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core)"] [528 1 "// ParseComplex is complex(s): \"1+2j\", \"-j\", \"(3e1-2.5j)\", \"inf\", surrounding whitespace."] [579 1 "// complexDeprecation is PyErr_WarnFormat(PyExc_DeprecationWarning, 1, msg): warnings.warn at the calling frame."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[36 25] [168 22] [168 45] [204 26] [294 64] [307 62] [314 27] [316 32] [318 30] [335 72] [348 86] [349 86] [412 23] [425 53] [429 28] [433 239] [444 27] [447 25] [460 28] [461 108] [467 28] [468 106] [474 28] [482 27] [547 24] [547 31]]} (go/file "complex.go" :imports [


